  "notes": [
    "rows[] transcribe the report's table cell by cell (likelihood, gpu_a100, cpu_many_core, laptop, secondary, rule_branches_on); the text is the human-readable source and is never parsed.",
    "tables[] and rows[].routes are the machine reading of those rows. scripts/misc/tooling/catalogue_lifecycle.py reads tables[] (and coverage_matrix.py reads both), so this file is the only copy of the table; test_coverage_matrix.py checks each route names the table catalogue_lifecycle.py dispatches to.",
    "Machine reading: host 'laptop' is the Laptop column; 'same' and 'as <row>' resolve to that row's setups; regime-only routes (_dft below 10,000 visibilities, _streaming at n_vis >= 1e7) are designated but not planned in the standard regime.",
    "Machine reading: a point-source likelihood has no linear operator, so its setups are spelled ..._na_... (R1) where the report writes jax_*_dense_fp64.",
    "Machine reading: the interferometer CPU many-core cell names a numba direct_conv vs FFT cost model; it is read as numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde until a designation decision names the route.",
    "Mixed precision is experimental everywhere at day zero (the report's footnote); a setup in no table is experimental.",
    "No designation decision exists yet: an 'optimal' here is provisional and is labelled class secondary with 'provisional_optimal: true' on records (R3); planned_cells carry it as optimal.",
    "Machine reading: instrument_scoped_setups[] plan a designated setup only on the listed instruments of its dataset types (catalogue_lifecycle.planned_setups); on any other instrument it stays designated but is not planned, like the regime-only suffixes. R1(a) (human 2026-10-25, autolens_profiling#469) scopes the dense pixelized interferometer NUFFT route to sma.",
    "Machine reading: a GPU setup (jax_gpu_*) is planned only on a host in gpu_hosts[]; on a GPU-less host (hpc_ral_cpu, laptop) it stays designated but is not planned, like the regime-only suffixes. A table lists a GPU setup on every host because the report's secondary column is host-agnostic (human 2026-10-29: fix the planner gap seen in 2c/2e/2g)."
  ],
  "footnote": "Mixed precision is `experimental` everywhere at day zero (the fp32 leg currently runs fp64: Mind bug draft). Compile cost is recorded where available but is not a class axis.",
